Z||000000||86GT-FstBk||07-09-2000||11:19 AM||||my 86 GT fastback body is splitting apart on the driver's side where the 1/4 panel meets the roof piece and it also caused my sail panel to crack too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> .  It first happened when I was jacking up the car.  The further I jacked it up the bigget the gap got.  I'm am jacking it up in the right place so could some one help me out on what the cause is and how to fix it. Thanx for your help in advance.||||reg||8
Z||000001||batboy||07-09-2000||12:04 PM||||I've seen several Fieros crack in that same area. It's caused from too much body flex.||||reg||1
Z||000002||86GT-FstBk||07-09-2000||05:56 PM||||thanks but I'm trying to get info on how to prevent this from happening anymore<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||07-09-2000||06:18 PM||||I told you it was caused from excessive body flex...duh...you have to reduce the amount of twisting your car does. Lots of miles on rough roads, hitting hard bumps too fast, high performance diving (racing), and even worn out chassis, cradle, and body mounting bushings can all lead to excessive flexing. To repair the damage correctly will require body panel replacement, after you fixed the flexing problem. Bondo or fiberglass filler will only be a temporary solution.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||07-10-2000||12:09 PM||||You can drive a square stock shaft into the frame rail and tie it to the front and back subframes like they do on the convertable Fiero's. I think coyote posted some pics on how he did his. If it removes flex for a convertable it should do fine for what you want.||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||07-11-2000||08:15 PM||||Good idea, Oreif. Early Camaros had a lot of body flex too, so I installed subframe connectors on my 68 RS/SS. Didn't even think about doing that with a Fiero.||||reg||1
